# test/gates.map: which suites a change needs (read by test/gates; the only place of these rules).
#
#   suite <path> <group> [needs=<a,b>] [-- <args>]   a suite, its group, what test/gates prepares for it, its arguments
#   set <name> <target>...                           a named list of targets (used as @name)
#   rule <glob> <target>...                          a changed file that matches <glob> needs these suites ("-": none)
#   fallback <target>...                             a changed file that matches no rule needs these
#
# A target is a suite's path, a glob over the suites' paths (test/wake-*.mjs), @set, or %group (every suite of that
# group). A changed file that is itself a suite runs that suite (no rule needed). Globs: * and ? stay inside one
# path segment, ** spans any number of them, and a glob ending in / or /** takes the whole folder. Every rule a file
# matches adds its suites (rules add up; none wins over another).
#
# Groups, and how test/gates runs them:
#   hermetic  throwaway HOME / MM_HOME and free ports only: in parallel with each other
#   ports     binds ports from a fixed range or starts real servers (Dolt, the gateway): one at a time
#   docker    throwaway containers (mm's Docker wrapper or rootless podman): one at a time
#   live      uses the machine (its mm, process manager, Paseo, web proxy): one at a time, after all the others,
#             never next to another suite; --no-live skips them (the result says "skipped (--no-live)", not pass)
# hermetic, ports and docker run at the same time as three lanes; within ports and within docker, one after another.
#
# Arguments may name what test/gates makes: {mm} (an mm built from the head, or --bin), {bd} {dolt} (the releases
# template/tools.json pins, checksums checked; or GATES_BD / GATES_DOLT), {old-template} (the base's template/).
# needs: mm (MM_BIN_DIR: a folder whose mm is that binary, first on PATH for a live suite), site (template/site's
# packages and one build before the suites start; they get BOARD_PHONE_NOBUILD=1, so no two build the site at once).

